    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "content": "## MB3R Resilience Posture\nThis is a **predicted resilience posture** view built from Bering-discovered topology and Sheaft analysis. It is not a raw health panel.\n\n### Read It In This Order\n1. **Policy Verdict**: current policy result for the latest report. Higher severity is worse: `pass -> warn -> fail -> error`.\n2. **Overall Posture**: cross-profile weighted posture score from `0` to `1`. Higher is better.\n3. **Report Age / Snapshot Age**: freshness indicators. Lower is better.\n4. **Simulated Availability by Profile**: `steady-state` is the baseline profile. The fault profiles are intentionally lower because they simulate degraded conditions.\n5. **Journey Availability by Profile**: the four target frontend journeys. `0` means the journey is currently missing or broken in the active trace-derived model.\n\n### Color Semantics\n- For posture and availability panels: **green is better, red is worse**.\n- For age panels: **green is fresher, red is staler**.\n\nRaw inputs remain available at `http://localhost:14318/metrics`, `http://localhost:19080/status`, and `http://localhost:19080/current-report`.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "What This Shows",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "webstore-metrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
